   "id": "ch02_07"
  },
  {
   "narration": "Two American presidents came to speak in its shadow. In 1963, John F. Kennedy declared: Ich bin ein Berliner. In 1987, Ronald Reagan stood near the Brandenburg Gate and said: Mr. Gorbachev, tear down this wall.",
